WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.830
OK, so I'm sure by now you all know what's
going on with voting in November.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:05.830
We should vote.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:11.420
The act of voting itself, whether you vote
in person or not, has become highly politicized.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.570
My take is everybody should vote.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:17.430
You have the opportunity to participate in
deciding who's going to lead our country and

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.680
not just talking about Trump versus Biden.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.350
I'm talking about the local level.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.779
I'm talking about the state level.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:25.440
And you should exercise that right.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.490
And you should have a say.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.660
So people have written to me and they've said,
David, with all of this confusion about absentee

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.890
versus vote by mail, please explain how to
vote by mail.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:40.690
So first of all, what we're talking about
for November is expanded absentee ballot access,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:46.190
or you might call it in some states, universal
absentee voting in states that have decided

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:48.170
to send ballots out.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.910
They go only to registered voters.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.040
They don't go to undocumented immigrants.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.290
They don't go to children.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.149
Do not fall for those talking points.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:00:59.890
Each state has its own rules.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.879
So you have to know the rules of your state
or commonwealth.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:06.100
So, first of all, figure out the rules in
your state.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.130
Go to the NASA s Web site page called absentee
and early voting.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:15.969
We're linking to that page in the description
to the YouTube clip for this story you put

00:01:15.969 --> 00:01:16.969
in your state.

00:01:16.969 --> 00:01:22.479
For example, when I put in Massachusetts,
it takes me to the Massachusetts secretary

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:26.689
of the commonwealth page with information
on how to get an absentee ballot.

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:32.139
Now, Massachusetts sent out absentee ballot
applications automatically.

00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:33.810
I received the application.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.460
If I plan to vote by mail, which I do, I fill
it out.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:37.509
I send it back in.

00:01:37.509 --> 00:01:41.299
And then at some point after the September
1st primary, once we know exactly who will

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:46.989
be on the ballot in November, I will get the
actual absentee ballot, which is where I vote.

00:01:46.989 --> 00:01:49.820
Now, this is not the situation in every state.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:55.989
If you look at the Brookings map raiding states
on vote by mail, you will see that states

00:01:55.989 --> 00:01:58.509
range in ratings from eight to F..

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:04.819
Right now, Alabama is the only state rated
F on absentee voting, while a bunch of states

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:06.020
get an A..

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:11.360
Including the three West Coast states, Utah,
Colorado, Hawaii and Washington, D.C., and

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.270
then a bunch of states get a B..

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:18.080
And this relates to the ease with which you
can access an absentee ballot in your particular

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.080
state.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:25.860
Now, I wish I could tell you this is the one
way to do this, but each state runs things

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.860
differently.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.040
So you actually do need to go and look at
your state's voting Web site.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.829
Now, a few things to understand.

00:02:31.829 --> 00:02:35.049
And again, your state's Web site will tell
you this.

00:02:35.049 --> 00:02:39.130
If you're in the Commonwealth of Virginia
or the state of Florida or even the state

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:43.940
of Florida, as Trump says, the every state
and commonwealth has a Web site that will

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:45.260
explain this to you.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.970
In some states, every registered voter will
get a ballot automatically.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.069
Perfect.

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:52.700
Just confirm your registered.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.750
You can do that on the USA dot gov page.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.590
Confirm you are registered to vote.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:58.790
We're also linking to that.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:02.319
If you're registered and you're in a state
that's sending out ballots to every registered

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:03.319
voter.

00:03:03.319 --> 00:03:04.319
Beautiful.

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:09.540
In other states, every registered voter will
be sent an application for a ballot which

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:15.390
you have to fill out and send in in order
to request the actual ballot be sent to you.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:22.799
That's what I did in Massachusetts, for example,
in some states, you have to choose to go and

00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:25.189
apply for an absentee ballot.

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:28.480
Now, typically, I think there are some states
where it can be.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:34.269
Online in other states, you have to send some
physical piece of mail to request the absentee

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:37.159
ballot in some states.

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:39.489
Everybody is allowed an absentee ballot.

00:03:39.489 --> 00:03:45.190
In other states, you have to give a valid
reason for why you want to vote absentee.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:51.099
And depending on your state saying I'm afraid
of catching Corona virus is considered a valid

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:52.099
reason.

00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:54.340
Now, in other states, there's still a fight
going on about that.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:59.389
So you would have to look at the reasons that
are considered valid reasons for requesting

00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:04.299
an absentee ballot in your state and match
it to your situation.

00:04:04.299 --> 00:04:09.959
I'm not suggesting anybody lie, but examine
what the valid reasons are and determine whether

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:13.450
any of them match your circumstances.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.819
It's tragic that this is what's going on.

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:22.639
But all we can do, given that voting in some
states starts in four and a half weeks, is

00:04:22.639 --> 00:04:24.440
to go to your state's Web site.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:29.030
If you have to request something, do it now
and stay on top of this.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.520
This really isn't difficult.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.599
And I understand when you hear, well, am I
getting a ballot or am I getting an application?

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:36.820
Do I have to print the application or can
I fill it out online?

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:37.820
I get it.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.710
We have 50 different systems in the United
States.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.060
All of the links you need are in the description
to this YouTube video clip.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.750
If anybody you know, is at all confused about
how to vote by mail.

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:50.750
Send them this clip.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:55.691
We did a story on the bonus show where we
discuss that a whole bunch of people, including

00:04:55.691 --> 00:05:00.300
and particularly young people, aren't sure
how to vote by mail, how to request an absentee

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.840
ballot or whether they will get one automatically.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.480
That's exactly the confusion we are trying
to resolve here.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.500
Figure out what's going on in your state using
the links provided in the description for

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.520
this YouTube clip.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.370
It is not difficult.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.910
You have a right to vote in most states.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.419
Now you have a right to vote absentee.

00:05:18.419 --> 00:05:23.289
If you go through the right process, take
advantage of things that are offered to you,

00:05:23.289 --> 00:06:37.310
because the stakes, quite frankly, could not
be higher.

